  "body": "Asked for by the maintainer in chat on 2026-11-16:\n\n> issue enhancement; all the \"voxel animation\" should not be realtime, it should be pre-calculation so it doesnt lag behind while playing the simulation.\n\nWhat happens now:\n\n- The simulation calculates the stock removal while the playback runs.\n- On a long or dense toolpath the stock picture comes later than the tool position. The animation lags.\n\nWhat is wanted:\n\n- The stock removal is calculated before the playback, not during it.\n- During playback the stock picture is at the tool position at each moment, at each playback speed, and when the user moves the time slider forward or back.\n\nPoints for the design (record the choices in `docs/decisions/`):\n\n- Where the calculation runs: a background job after generation, or at the first press of Play, with a progress display and a cancel control. The UI must not stop during it.\n- What is stored: stock states at fixed steps of the program (keyframes) plus a fast replay between them, or a full list of states. Give the memory limit and what happens when a job exceeds it.\n- When the stored result becomes invalid: an edit of the operation, the tool, the stock, the fixture or the setup. Use the same stamp that the operation cache uses, so that an old stock picture is never shown for a new toolpath.\n- The result is ephemeral UI state. It does not go into the project file and it is not a command.\n- All resources of an operation are freed when the operation is deleted (AGENTS.md, delete hooks).\n- The verify step and the checks that can block the post do not change. This work changes the display only. The PR pins that.\n- Related: #2177 (traced playback refuses a rotated stock), #586 / #637 (stock on the field engine).\n\nDone means:\n\n- A test pins that, after the calculation, the stock state at a given program position is the same as the state that the present real-time simulation reaches there.\n- A test pins that a jump of the time slider (forward and back) shows the correct stock state without a new full calculation.\n- A test pins that an edit of the operation makes the stored result invalid.\n- A reading on one large fixture shows the calculation time and the memory use, in the PR body.\n",
